   $q$Solve $y = \frac{2x + k}{m}$ for $x$, where $m \neq 0$:$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = \\frac{my}{2} - k$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-only-one-term"},{"text":"$x = \\frac{my - k}{2}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$x = \\frac{my + k}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-moving-term"},{"text":"$x = \\frac{m(y - k)}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"undid-operations-in-wrong-order"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = \frac{my - k}{2}$$q$, $q$Multiply both sides by $m$: $my = 2x + k$. Subtract $k$: $my - k = 2x$. Divide by $2$: $x = \frac{my - k}{2}$. The choice $x = \frac{m(y - k)}{2}$ subtracts $k$ before clearing the fraction, but $k$ is divided by $m$ along with $2x$, so the $m$ must be cleared first.$q$, 'draft', null)
