   $q$The art club has 84 dollars and adds 6.50 dollars each week. The chess club has 120 dollars and spends 2.50 dollars each week. After how many weeks will the two clubs have the same amount of money?$q$, $q$[{"text":"9","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-rates-instead-of-adding"},{"text":"4","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-the-quotient"},{"text":"36","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-divide-by-rate"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$4$q$, $q$Set the amounts equal: $84 + 6.5w = 120 - 2.5w$. Add $2.5w$ and subtract $84$: $9w = 36$, so $w = 4$. Check: $84 + 26 = 110$ and $120 - 10 = 110$. The choice 9 divides 36 by $6.5 - 2.5 = 4$, but the chess club's money goes down, so the weekly gap closes by $6.5 + 2.5 = 9$ dollars.$q$, 'draft', null)
